			}]
		}
		{
			title: "Cute Doll"
			icon: {
				id: "the_vault:vault_doll"
				Count: 1b
				tag: { }
			}
			x: 3.75d
			y: 1.0d
			shape: "rsquare"
			subtitle: "It's Staring At Me"
			description: [
				"&dIf you have some Assistants with you, but you aren't all able to run Vaults at the same rate, you might want to look into &lVault Dolls."
				""
				"&5Ye can have an Assistant make a Vault Doll, and it'll bear their name and character skin. "
				""
				"&dEquip the doll on your head Curios slot. Make sure you aren't in a Vault Party with your Assistant, nor should they enter the Vault either. Then run the Vault. It'll randomly 'copy' some of the loot you collect and store it in itself."
				""
				"&5After the Vault, give the doll back to the friend. They can Right Click the Doll onto the ground to release it. CAREFUL, do this in an enclosed area!"
				""
				"&dSee, when you 'release' the doll, it starts to run around. To get your loot, you gotta kill it."
				""
				"&lServers can disable placing Vault Dolls and require using Doll Blenders, as Vault Dolls with high amounts of loot can crash servers. Change the gamerule enablePlacingVaultDolls to false!"
			]
			hide_dependency_lines: true
			dependencies: ["76B7D44E338DC9B7"]
			hide: true
			id: "49C50AC9021411A0"
			tasks: [{
				id: "0F2B6CC25BD24BAD"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
		}
		{
			title: "Safe Doll Extraction"
			icon: "woldsvaults:doll_dismantler"
			x: 4.75d
			y: 1.0d
			shape: "rsquare"
			subtitle: "Will It Blend?"
			description: [
				"&dTo retrieve the goods gathered by Vault Dolls, you'll usually deploy the doll and then kill the doll as it tries to run away."
				""
				"&5Aye, and this  can cause issues, Bandit, cause if the doll contains tons of items, it can 'lag' the server. Or if the Assistant lags and the doll escapes."
				""
				"&dSo, the Doll Blender is a simple, if slighlty morbid, solution! Set it down, insert Vault Doll, Blend Vault Doll, and the Blender holds the loot so you can retrieve it at a safer pace."
			]
			hide_dependency_lines: true
			dependencies: ["49C50AC9021411A0"]
			id: "59F111F615EEAC31"
			tasks: [{
				id: "46C0C69B5C61E37F"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
		}
		{
			title: "Just Like New"
			x: -6.5d
			y: -3.5d
			shape: "rsquare"
			subtitle: "Ignore The Scuff Marks"
			description: [
				"&5As you level higher, you will slow down in gaining levels, but increase the amount of equipment you find in a Vault."
				""
				"&5Eventually you'll find a piece of equipment that should last you long enough that you wear down the Durability to the breaking point."
				""
				"&5If you still have a piece of Gear you want to use longer when the Durability runs out, you'll want a Repair Core."
				""
				"&5Combine a Repair Core with the piece of equipment in an Anvil to repair it. It will consume a Repair slot on the equipment and refill the Durability."
			]
